---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="Privacy policy" description="The privacy policy of Lone Voice." updated="22 November 2026">
  <p>
    This page explains what happens to information about you when you read Lone Voice. In short: this site
    doesn't ask you for any, and doesn't try to collect it.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing from you directly. There are no accounts, comments, forms or newsletter sign-ups, so you never
    have to give a name, an email address or anything else to read here.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The site sets no cookies.</li>
    <li>It stores nothing in your browser.</li>
    <li>It runs no analytics, advertising or tracking tools.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where the site is hosted</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. When you open a page, your device asks Cloudflare's servers for it,
    so Cloudflare receives technical details such as your IP address, your browser type and the page you asked
    for. Every website works this way, and Cloudflare handles that information under its own privacy policy. I
    don't collect or keep it myself.
  </p>

  <h2>Fonts, images and search</h2>
  <p>
    The fonts and images are served from this site, not from another company, so nothing is requested from a
    third party when a page loads. The search box works inside your browser: the words you type are not sent
    to anyone and are not stored.
  </p>

  <h2>Links and share buttons</h2>
  <p>
    The share buttons for Facebook, X, Telegram and WhatsApp do nothing until you press one. Then your browser
    opens that service in a new tab with this page's address, and that service's own privacy policy applies.
    Links to other websites work the same way: once you leave, I have no control over what that site does.
  </p>

  <h2>The RSS feed</h2>
  <p>
    The RSS feed is a plain file that your feed reader downloads. I don't keep a list of subscribers.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this changes, for example if I ever add analytics, I will update this page first, and the date at the
    top will change with it.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
